@host = http://localhost:5081
@customer = 10000000-0000-4000-8000-019a6a000001

### Run in Development; field/option IDs below assume a fresh demo database.
GET {{host}}/api/customers

### Global text field
POST {{host}}/api/custom-fields
Content-Type: application/json

{"fieldKey":"external_reference","label":"External reference","fieldType":"TEXT","options":[]}

### Global dropdown
POST {{host}}/api/custom-fields
Content-Type: application/json

{"fieldKey":"customer_segments","label":"Customer segments","fieldType":"MULTI_SELECT","options":[{"label":"VIP","sortOrder":1},{"label":"Retail","sortOrder":2},{"label":"Wholesale","sortOrder":3}]}

### Both fields appear even without assigned values
GET {{host}}/api/customers/{{customer}}/custom-fields

### First assignment; no row expected
PUT {{host}}/api/customers/{{customer}}/custom-fields/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"textValue":null,"selectedOptionIds":[1,3],"expectedVersion":null}

### Whole-set replacement; expect version1
PUT {{host}}/api/customers/{{customer}}/custom-fields/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"textValue":null,"selectedOptionIds":[2,3],"expectedVersion":1}

### Same set, reverse order: changed=false, stays version2
PUT {{host}}/api/customers/{{customer}}/custom-fields/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"textValue":null,"selectedOptionIds":[3,2],"expectedVersion":2}

### Two transitions, actor1, UTC timestamps
GET {{host}}/api/customers/{{customer}}/custom-fields/2/history

### New customers receive global definitions with unset values
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Customer C"}
